<item>
            <title>[LU-20897] lfsck: slave PFID repair passes arguments out of order</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20897</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;lfsck_layout_slave_repair_pfid() calls __lfsck_layout_update_pfid() with its last three arguments out of order:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; __lfsck_layout_update_pfid(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; struct lu_env *env,
				      struct lfsck_component *com,
				      struct dt_object *child,
				      &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; struct lu_fid *pfid,
				      &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; struct ost_layout *ol, __u32 offset,
				      __u32 version, __u32 range)
...
	rc = __lfsck_layout_update_pfid(env, com, obj,
					&amp;amp;lrl-&amp;gt;lrl_ff_client.ff_parent,
					&amp;amp;lrl-&amp;gt;lrl_ff_client.ff_layout,
					lrl-&amp;gt;lrl_ff_client.ff_layout_version,
					lrl-&amp;gt;lrl_ff_client.ff_range,
					lrl-&amp;gt;lrl_ff_client.ff_parent.f_ver);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The layout version is passed as the stripe index (offset), the range as the layout version, and the stripe index (ff_parent.f_ver) as the range.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This came in with 36ba989752c (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10288&quot; title=&quot;LFSCK support for mirrored files&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-10288&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10288&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; lfsck: layout LFSCK for mirrored file&quot;), which added the version and range parameters after offset but inserted the new arguments ahead of f_ver at this caller. The other callers pass them in order.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the OST-side PFID repair: when the OST finds that a client&apos;s PFID for an object differs from the one stored and the MDT confirms the client&apos;s is right, the OST rewrites the object&apos;s filter_fid from lrl_ff_client. ofd_add_inconsistency_item() leaves ff_layout_version and ff_range zero there, so the rewritten filter_fid gets stripe index 0, layout version 0 and a range equal to the real stripe index. For any stripe other than 0, the &quot;repaired&quot; object then names the wrong stripe index, which a later layout LFSCK reports as an unmatched pair, and orphan recovery would put it in the wrong slot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: pass ff_parent.f_ver as offset, then ff_layout_version and ff_range.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found during review of &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/62389&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/62389&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19566&quot; title=&quot;FLR-EC: mark EC OST objects for LFSCK, rebuild EC components&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19566&quot;&gt;LU-19566&lt;/a&gt;), which extends the same call.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
